From f68a5d0229f47a71ca125c32f472aedf359753a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 15:35:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 020/638] base: fix IDMap iterator assignment member names
 [chromium] [gcc]

AI_PHASE: chromium-headless-bringup

AI_STATUS: done

ROOT_CAUSE: IDMap::Iterator's copy-assignment operator referenced nonexistent iter.map and iter.iter members. Chromium's usual Clang path left the dormant template body unchecked, while GCC 15 validates it and stopped the AROS cross-build.

FIX_REASON: Use the actual private members map_ and iter_, matching the already-correct copy constructor and the intended iterator-depth bookkeeping.

SCOPE: base/containers IDMap iterator copy assignment.

VALIDATION: ninja -C out/aros-headless -j4 obj/ipc/ipc/message_router.o

RISK: low; this is a direct typo correction in previously ill-formed code.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
---
 base/containers/id_map.h | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/base/containers/id_map.h b/base/containers/id_map.h
index 4ff5ee7c8b..f84c7c5c6f 100644
--- a/base/containers/id_map.h
+++ b/base/containers/id_map.h
@@ -178,8 +178,8 @@ class IDMap final {
     }
 
     const Iterator& operator=(const Iterator& iter) {
-      map_ = iter.map;
-      iter_ = iter.iter;
+      map_ = iter.map_;
+      iter_ = iter.iter_;
       Init();
       return *this;
     }
